            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-HVaUdq9pjop4TzxluYFlMz4sgfg\">Looking at the sports that showed an overall increase, in 1995, football led with 41% of respondents showing interest, while swimming attracted 22% and rugby 24%. Football maintained its dominant position with a steady rise, reaching 44% by 2005. Swimming saw more substantial changes, increasing to 29% in 2000 before slightly declining to 27% in the final year, while rugby showed notable fluctuation, dropping to 19% in 2000 before recovering strongly to 27% by 2005.</div>\n</div>",
